# PHYS 3810: full-course local preview v0.2.0-rc1

**Unpublished local preview.** This folder contains setup and five bounded
quantum-algorithm lessons. It is not a published student release or final
classroom approval. Session coverage, assessment, delivery arrangements,
required platforms, and human pacing remain provisional.

Source commit: `{{SOURCE_COMMIT}}`.
Local archive: `{{ASSET_NAME}}`.

## Start here

1. Extract the complete `phys3810-fa2026` folder and open a terminal there.
2. Follow the [student setup guide](teaching/phys3810-fa2026/handouts/FULL_COURSE_SETUP_DRAFT.md)
   or its [four-page review-draft PDF](teaching/phys3810-fa2026/handouts/PHYS3810_Full_Course_Student_Setup_v0.1_REVIEW_DRAFT.pdf).
3. Use 64-bit CPython 3.12 and the supplied pinned requirements/constraints.
4. Run `python scripts/validate_classroom.py` from this folder.
5. Open [preflight](teaching/phys3810-fa2026/notebooks/00_setup_preflight.ipynb),
   then use the [lesson index](teaching/phys3810-fa2026/COURSE_PLAN.md).

The required inventory is **160 tests, eight notebooks, 50 nonempty code cells,
and 16 PNG figures**. All required cells, including expansion/reference cells,
must execute without errors. See [validation and limits](VALIDATION.md) for
what the checks establish. The builder does not execute the runtime checks;
the separate extraction receipt records whether this particular ZIP passed.

Installation needs internet access. Default execution afterward is local and
credential-free; no Git installation, IBM account, GPU, or quantum hardware
is needed. Do not mix packages from another Python environment or update the
supplied pins during a lesson.

## Scope and document editions

The lessons cover Grover on 2–5 qubits; exact QFT on 1–6 qubits; QPE with 1–6
counting qubits and one/two targets; exact-spectrum positive-Hermitian 2x2 HHL;
and a compiled full-domain N=15 Shor example with four residue qubits. These
are small instructional examples, without claims of general scalability or
quantum advantage.

The supplied student PDF is **document v0.1 REVIEW DRAFT** for proposed
**code v0.2.0-rc1**. Its delivered bytes are unchanged. It is distinct from the
older Grover-only code preview and document-v0.2 guides. The future full-course
student download remains unpublished; no download URL is asserted here.

Instructor guides, instructor PDFs, and presenter answer sheets are excluded.
The notebooks, mathematical contracts, and tests still contain worked results
and expected answers. This is **not an answer-free assessment package**; follow
the instructor's eventual collaboration, solution, and submission directions.

Native Windows x64, macOS ARM64/Intel, and native editor UI remain untested.
Windows ARM64 and 32-bit Python are outside the stated target. The demonstrated
Ubuntu/JupyterLab path and its limitations are described in the setup guide.

## File identity

[MANIFEST.json](MANIFEST.json) records the source revision, file hashes, modes,
expected validation counts, and disclosed standalone-document adaptations.
Runtime source, tests, eight notebook files, dependencies, license, lint
configuration, and both student-guide files retain exact committed bytes.
Technical contracts retain their mathematical/API/acceptance bodies; their
repository status/history framing is omitted. This README, setup pointer,
lesson index, and validation page provide standalone navigation.

There are no environments, credentials, Git metadata, generated execution
outputs, prompts, policy/chat records, old archives, or instructor answer
documents in this archive. The manifest excludes itself; the archive checksum
in its separate build receipt identifies the complete ZIP.
